//? Title: B* Multi-Goal Best-First Search

\toc

> Mathematics

Here B\* follows the list's graph-search meaning: find the least-cost member of
a goal set.  A lower bound \(h(v)\) estimates cost to the nearest goal, and
the frontier is ordered by \(g+h\).  If \(h\) is admissible for the goal set,
the first removed goal is globally cheapest by the same lower-bound proof as
A\*.

```
mark every allowed goal
best-first search from start by path-cost + goal-set lower bound
stop at the first removed goal
```

> C\+\+ example

```{cpp, results="output", exports="both", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/algorithms/tour_search.hpp>
#include <iostream>
int main(){auto r=datamunge::algorithms::b_star_search(
4,{{0,1,1},{1,2,5},{0,3,2}},0,{2,3},{2,5,0,0});std::cout<<r.path.back();}
```
// result_begin:
// 3
// result_end

It selects goal 3 at cost 2.
